// Nothing. Deliberately.
//
// Upstream's LanguageSelect renders its <starlight-lang-select> only when
// `config.isMultilingual`, and this site has one locale — so the element never
// appeared on any page. Its <script> did: Astro hoists scripts from the import
// graph, not from what renders, so all 18 pages shipped a custom-element
// registration for an element that is never there.
//
// Overriding the component removes it from the graph, so the chunk is never
// emitted. This is the only Starlight script this wave deletes rather than
// externalises — the other three drive chrome that really is on the page.
//
// Restoring it is one line: drop this override from `components:` in
// astro.config.mjs the day the site gains a second locale.
